./LOGBOOK.md:584:- SCOPE: `curator-spec` rc.5 candidate, task worktree `.temp/TASK-260728-1g0z69/curator-spec-worktree`. Still exactly three files: `decisions/0007-compiled-build-toolchain-preflight.md`, `docs/compiled-build-toolchain-requirements.md`, one `CHANGELOG.md` bullet. Vector inventory 40 → 58 cases. `conformance/v1` and `release/1.0.0-rc.5.json` byte-identical to the accepted predecessor after regeneration.
./LOGBOOK.md:594:- DECISION: the effective requirement is a **gate, not a build input** — same reasoning that kept host capability evidence out of the key in decision 0006. No bypass exists because Stage A gates before cache lookup. Consequence: zero frozen artifacts change (`curator-go-toolchain-v1`, receipts v1/v2, markers v2/v3, rc.4 digests, every published cache key), and adopting the contract causes no rebuild.
./LOGBOOK.md:596:- NOTE: `make regenerate-check` cannot pass inside a task worktree carrying the uncommitted rc.5 candidate — it runs `git diff --exit-code` against `57c1f56`. Prove determinism instead by diffing regenerated `conformance/v1` against the accepted predecessor and by running the gate twice in a clean `git init` probe.
./LOGBOOK.md:597:- SCOPE: `curator-spec` @ `57c1f56` + rc.5 candidate. Two new files (`decisions/0007-compiled-build-toolchain-preflight.md`, `docs/compiled-build-toolchain-requirements.md`) plus one CHANGELOG bullet. No schema, vector, or generated byte changed.
./LOGBOOK.md:602:- FINDING: `TASK-260728-2kp3tv`. The `curator-build` stem names **two unrelated things** in the rc.5 candidate. `curator-build.json` is the schema-7 repository-root descriptor (unreleased, renameable). `curator-build-source-v1` is the schema-6 **build-source snapshot digest algorithm** — the domain-separation prefix hashed over the frozen external snapshot, defined at `schemas/v1/common.schema.json:303` and referenced 113 times.
./LOGBOOK.md:603:- FINDING: the digest algorithm is bound into rc.4 byte-frozen artifacts. `conformance/v1/schema-cases/install-marker-v2/valid.json` carries it and is digest-pinned at `538d12bb89d2...` by `TestRC4CompiledArtifactsRemainByteFrozen` (`tools/generate-vectors/main_test.go`). A naive `s/curator-build/skill-build/g` breaks the schemas-1-6 byte freeze and fails that guard.
./LOGBOOK.md:605:- DECISION: renamed the descriptor family only (`curator-build.json`, `curator-build-v1{,.schema.json}`, `curatorBuildTargetV1`, two generator helpers); left the digest-algorithm namespace untouched. All nine rc.4 frozen digests re-verified unchanged.
./LOGBOOK.md:608:- SCOPE: `curator-spec` @ `57c1f56` + rc.5 candidate; 71 files, one schema file and one schema-case directory renamed. New candidate pin `sha256:9ba9b8ec…`.
./LOGBOOK.md:613:- ANOMALY: the accepted `TASK-260728-zb2s4z` outcome artifact reports the rc.5 candidate protocol pin as `sha256:bfe49f25…`. The predecessor worktree on disk pins `sha256:58f8d229…` in both `candidate_protocol_pin.manifest_sha256` and `downstream_consumption.required_manifest_sha256`, and `shasum -a 256 conformance/v1/manifest.json` confirms `58f8d229…`.
./LOGBOOK.md:777:- EVIDENCE: local macOS arm64 build/vet/gofmt/full/`-race`/rc.5/rc.4/real-build/scoped-lint all exit 0. macOS amd64 (`ssh relux`) and Windows amd64 (`ssh win`) verified byte-identical (143 `cmd`+`internal` Go files, per-file SHA-256 diff clean) with build, vet, task packages under the rc.5 root, and the real vendored build all exit 0. Windows `go test ./...` still exits non-zero in the same five pre-existing packages outside this task.
./LOGBOOK.md:782:- DECISION: dropped the old `source_not_readonly` permission-bit gate. rc.5 defines the portable source mechanism as frozen snapshot + identity re-verification; a permission-bit rejection would be an extra containment claim the portable profile may not make.
./LOGBOOK.md:788:- EVIDENCE: portable cache key reproduces `sha256:529370122ae11e2e961d5265b1a020e046bcd43165b2eb96b05e73a51187ac9b`; canonical receipt is byte-identical to the accepted `schema-cases/build-receipt-v1/valid.json`. 222 cases pass under the rc.5 root. Green on macOS arm64 (incl. `-race`), macOS amd64, and Windows amd64 — all three with a real Go 1.25.5 vendored build that is verified and never started.
./LOGBOOK.md:790:- NOTE: Linux is out of `rc5-native-control-inventory-v1`, so the driver rejects there with `build_execution_control_unavailable` before the worker. Linux coverage is compile/vet/test-link plus that rejection path only; no Linux host was used.
./LOGBOOK.md:795:- VERDICT: R2 is closed by the exhaustive `rc5-native-control-inventory-v1`, closed `capability-evidence-v1` vocabulary and per-platform examples, stable contradiction diagnostics, and negative guards. Official Apple and Microsoft API documentation supports the named native primitives without upgrading them into hardened platform claims.
./LOGBOOK.md:796:- EVIDENCE: 42 schemas / 422 manifest files, 22 Python tests, focused dishonest-evidence mutations, Go tests, vet, gofmt, compileall, generator build, two clean deterministic regenerations, and clean `make release-check VERSION=1.0.0-rc.5` passed independently.
./LOGBOOK.md:805:- FIX: "every native control the host actually provides" replaced by the exhaustive versioned `rc5-native-control-inventory-v1` inventory (5 controls, closed per-platform `{availability, mechanism, unavailable_reason}` records) and the closed `capability-evidence-v1` record (exact fields, states, `pre-worker-launch` probe timing, per-operation probe scope, result-only exposure, 8 consistency rules).
./LOGBOOK.md:806:- DECISION: extending the inventory is a specification revision with a new inventory version, NOT an execution-policy revision — inventory membership never enters a build input, artifact, or hashed identity. Both versions are pinned in `release/1.0.0-rc.5.json` and gated by `tools/release_gate.py`.
./LOGBOOK.md:814:- DECISION: curator-spec rc.5 `go-v1`/`go-repository-v1` now declare a named execution policy, `manager-worker-v1`, implemented on macOS and Windows. Replaces the earlier `TASK-260720-1zntv0` proposal of hardened-Linux-only real builds with `host_profile_unsupported` everywhere else.
./LOGBOOK.md:818:- FINDING: binding `execution_policy` into `goBuildPolicyV1` necessarily changes every `go-v1` logical cache key, so the rc.4 receipt example `93217cf1...` could not stay byte-frozen. Handled by moving it out of `TestRC4CompiledArtifactsRemainByteFrozen` into a dedicated non-alias guard that pins the old digest as negative evidence.
./LOGBOOK.md:819:- FINDING: marker v2 keeps its frozen rc.4 record shape. Its execution-policy binding is transitive through the recorded cache key and `receipt_sha256`, which is sufficient — a record written under one execution contract cannot validate against another.
./LOGBOOK.md:821:- NOTE: rc.5 candidate pin moved from `sha256:33fd7aed...` to `sha256:bfe49f25...`. Suite grew 411 → 422 files. Candidate still emits zero claim-v3 tuples.
