.resources/TASK-260720-cw39jh/TASK-260720-cw39jh_review-accepted.md-1-# Review verdict: accepted
.resources/TASK-260720-cw39jh/TASK-260720-cw39jh_review-accepted.md-2-
.resources/TASK-260720-cw39jh/TASK-260720-cw39jh_review-accepted.md:3:The compiled manager lifecycle vectors satisfy the task acceptance criteria and fit the accepted rc.4 manager architecture. Review compared the task worktree against accepted TASK-260720-1s1vr6 and confirmed the task-only delta is exactly tools/generate-vectors/main.go, tools/generate-vectors/main_test.go, conformance/v1/vectors/manager-lifecycle.json, and conformance/v1/manifest.json; no normative prose or release documentation differs.
.resources/TASK-260720-cw39jh/TASK-260720-cw39jh_review-accepted.md-4-
.resources/TASK-260720-cw39jh/TASK-260720-cw39jh_review-accepted.md-5-Coverage confirmed: ordered snapshot/dual-manifest/closure/collision/audit/registry/attestation gates before cache or build; provider-first and Unicode-scalar lexical command ordering; compiled dry-run prohibition and non-mutation matrix; private staging and second-build failure isolation; protected publication, identical-winner race, determinism mismatch, corruption, and untrusted-boundary outcomes; cross-project success and rollback isolation; deterministic locks and target order; consumer-last commit and reverse rollback; global-journal recovery; currentness, rebuild repair, and locked GC. Identity fields exactly reuse build-drivers.json portable_identity, and build-drivers.json remains byte-identical to the predecessor baseline.
.resources/TASK-260720-poa3ze/TASK-260720-poa3ze_compile-only-build-drivers.md-16-6. **Do not generalize this into “run a build tool.”** Cargo build scripts and procedural macros, SwiftPM manifests/plugins, Make/CMake/Meson commands, Maven/Gradle plugins, MSBuild tasks, npm lifecycle scripts, JavaScript bundler configs/loaders/plugins, Python build backends, and similar mechanisms can execute package-selected host code during a build. Those violate the invariant by construction.
.resources/TASK-260720-poa3ze/TASK-260720-poa3ze_compile-only-build-drivers.md-17-7. **The current managers expose pre-existing lifecycle issues that the build change must not copy forward.** Both record a consumer before materialization and both trust an existing runtime cache directory without verifying its required paths. The Python dry-run also appears able to mutate audit-registry cache/state before returning. These are implementation findings, not reasons to weaken the proposed contract.
.resources/TASK-260720-poa3ze/TASK-260720-poa3ze_compile-only-build-drivers.md:18:8. **Publish the feature as protocol `1.0.0-rc.4` with conformance claim schema 2.** Freeze claim schema 1 as historical rc.3 evidence; current rc.4 writers emit `conformance-claim-v2`, and current readers distinguish the two versions rather than rewriting the meaning of the v1 schema URL.
