.resources/TASK-260728-2spy93/TASK-260728-2spy93_review-verdict.md-7-1. The next wire shapes contradict the shared toolchain contract. Decision 0008 lines 194-202 says a schema-8 local command contains exactly `type`, `driver`, and `source_dir`. Lines 230-241 say descriptor schema 2 changes only the driver union, adds no member, and forbids a toolchain version. The current decision 0007 lines 343-346 requires a REQUIRED `toolchain` object in the next manifest schema and an OPTIONAL descriptor-target requirement in the next `skill-build.json` schema, with this task owning their version numbers. Decision 0008 references that contract but leaves no legal location for either object. This makes downstream TASK-260728-2jaw7h/TASK-260728-251p01 impossible without violating one accepted decision. Rework must synchronize both decisions and fix the exact closed local and descriptor target shapes while retaining the ban on paths, URLs, channels, install commands, arbitrary argv/environment, and trust roots.
