.resources/TASK-260728-2spy93/TASK-260728-2spy93_review-verdict.md:9:2. `manager-worker-v1` is semantically widened while claimed unchanged. Decision 0006 lines 39-58 fixes the identity to the Go-specific graph and exactly one `go list` plus one `go build`; its lines 131-133 state that a process-graph semantic change requires cache-identity separation. Decision 0008 lines 293-326 instead gives the same identity a driver-generic launcher/toolchain graph and driver-defined graph/compile commands. The assertion at lines 311-316 that the lower nodes were always per-operation values is not supported by the frozen definition. The rejected-alternative claim at lines 503-506 is also false as stated: a new policy identity for only new drivers need not change any Go cache key or rc.5 byte. Rework must either preserve Go on `manager-worker-v1` and version the new-driver policy, or provide a versioned composition model that proves the old policy meaning and Go semantics are not reinterpreted.
